# ============================================================================
# Magnanimous monorepo
#
# Rule of thumb: source and the media the apps need to RUN are committed.
# Dependencies, build output, credentials and the multi-gigabyte production
# masters are not.
# ============================================================================

# ---- dependencies & build output ----
node_modules/
.next/
out/
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo/
.cache/

# ---- credentials. Never commit these. ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.vercel/
*.pem
*.key
*-service-account*.json
credentials*.json

# ---- production masters (gigabytes; live in Drive / Blob, not git) ----
# tiki-lounge's own README is explicit that these stay out of the deployment.
tiki-lounge/audio-source/
tiki-lounge/design/
magnanimis/tmp/
magnanimis-labels/tmp/

# Encoded Cast ladders are regenerated by scripts/build-cast-*.sh
tiki-lounge/public/cast-media/
tiki-lounge/public/cast-hls/

# ---- independently versioned ----
# `magnanimis/` is its own repository with its own history and remote:
#   https://github.com/gemothy/magnanimis
# Committing it here would either swallow those 71 commits or leave an empty
# gitlink in every clone. Clone it separately alongside this one.
/magnanimis/

# `magnanimis-labels/` is a linked git WORKTREE of that same repository — its `.git`
# is a pointer file, not a directory. Same reasoning: already versioned, already
# pushed, and it would land here as an empty gitlink.
/magnanimis-labels/

# ---- os / editor noise ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---- logs ----
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ---- gone-away render output ----
# Frames written by the capture block in gone-away/index.html, via scripts/serve.ps1.
# These are working output for the art-direction review loop -- a couple of megabytes
# each and regenerated constantly -- not deliverables. reference/ is kept; renders/ is not.
/gone-away/renders/
